The '''2023 UEFA Europa Conference League final''' was the final match of the [[2022–23 UEFA Europa Conference League]], the second season of Europe's tertiary club [[association football|football]] tournament organised by [[UEFA]]. The match was played at the [[Fortuna Arena]] in [[Prague]], Czech Republic, on 7 June 2023,<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/026b-12cc960662f6-a33fcea5d68a-1000/20210719_circular_2021_51_en.zip |title=International match calendar and access list for 2022/23 |magazine=UEFA Circular Letter |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |number=51/2021 |date=19 July 2021 |access-date=5 November 2021}}</ref><ref name="host appointment">{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0275-151c90ada680-6a76591a389a-1000/ |title=UEFA EURO 2024 match schedule approved |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=10 May 2022 |access-date=10 May 2022}}</ref> between Italian club [[ACF Fiorentina|Fiorentina]] and English club [[West Ham United F.C.|West Ham United]].

West Ham United won the match 2–1 for their first UEFA Europa Conference League title.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaconferenceleague/news/0282-1833ad184f9c-3bd42a7f4d8e-1000/ |title=Fiorentina 1–2 West Ham: Bowen arrows Hammers to glory |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=7 June 2023 |access-date=7 June 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65826820 |title=Fiorentina 1–2 West Ham United: Jarrod Bowen goal decides Europa Conference League final |work=[[BBC Sport]] |date=7 June 2023 |access-date=8 June 2023}}</ref> As winners, they qualified for the group stage of the [[2023–24 UEFA Europa League]].

==Background==
This was the first appearance in the final of the competition for both teams. However, both [[ACF Fiorentina|Fiorentina]] and [[West Ham United F.C.|West Ham United]] had won the [[UEFA Cup Winners' Cup|Cup Winners' Cup]] in the 1960s; Fiorentina was its first winners back in [[1960–61 European Cup Winners' Cup|1960–61]], while West Ham won the cup [[1964–65 European Cup Winners' Cup|four seasons later]]. In addition, West Ham was one of the three winners of the [[1999 UEFA Intertoto Cup]]. Both clubs were also aiming to end their decades-long trophy drought; Fiorentina were looking to win their first trophy since winning the [[2000–01 Coppa Italia|Coppa Italia 22 years earlier]], while West Ham's most recent major title came in the [[1979–80 FA Cup]], when they became the most recent non-top flight side to win the tournament.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65809722|title=Europa Conference League final: Everything you need to know as West Ham play Fiorentina|website=BBC.com|date=6 June 2023|access-date=7 June 2023|archive-date=13 June 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230613063530/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65809722|url-status=live}}</ref>

This was Fiorentina's fifth European final, having won the Cup Winners' Cup in [[1961 European Cup Winners' Cup final|1961]] as well as losing the [[1957 European Cup final|1957 European Cup]], the [[1962 European Cup Winners' Cup final|1962 European Cup Winners' Cup]], and the [[1990 UEFA Cup final|1990 UEFA Cup]] finals. With this, they became the first team to reach the finals of all major UEFA club competitions.{{refn|group=note|European Cup/Champions League, Cup Winners' Cup, UEFA Cup/Europa League, UEFA Europa Conference League.}}<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://keepup.com.au/news/fiorentina-focus-a-look-at-west-hams-europa-conference-league-final-opponents/|title=Fiorentina focus – a look at West Ham's Europa Conference League final opponents|website=KeepUp.com.au |date=6 June 2023 |access-date=7 June 2023|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230609044233/https://keepup.com.au/news/fiorentina-focus-a-look-at-west-hams-europa-conference-league-final-opponents/|archive-date=9 June 2023}}</ref>

This was West Ham's third European final, having won the Cup Winners' Cup in [[1965 European Cup Winners' Cup final|1965]] as well as losing the [[1976 European Cup Winners' Cup final]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaconferenceleague/news/0281-18229e922c32-92fc7e8bba20-1000--fiorentina-vs-west-ham-final-facts/|title=Fiorentina vs West Ham final facts |website=UEFA.com|publisher=UEFA |date=22 May 2023 |access-date=7 June 2023|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230522182815/https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaconferenceleague/news/0281-181294ad033b-8e381d3c8062-1000--europa-conference-league-final-fiorentina-vs-west-ham-what-/|archive-date=22 May 2023}}</ref> They were the English team with the longest European major trophy drought—58 years since their latest triumph. Their defender [[Emerson Palmieri]] was aiming to become the first player to win [[UEFA club competition records and statistics#List of players to have won the three main European club competitions|all three currently existing major European trophies]], having won the [[2018–19 UEFA Europa League]] and the [[2020–21 UEFA Champions League]] with [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]].

==Venue==
[[File:Synot Tip Arena - Viktoria Plzen - FC Barcelona 0-4.jpg|thumb|275px|The [[Fortuna Arena]] in [[Prague]] hosted the final.]]

The Fortuna Arena previously hosted the [[2013 UEFA Super Cup]], as well as four matches at the [[2015 UEFA European Under-21 Championship]], including the [[2015 UEFA European Under-21 Championship Final|final]].

===Host selection===
A bidding process was launched by UEFA to select the venues of the finals of the UEFA Europa Conference League for both [[2022 UEFA Europa Conference League Final|2022]] and 2023. Associations interested in hosting one of the finals had until 20 February 2020 to submit bid dossiers.

The decision was originally scheduled to be made by the UEFA Executive Committee during their meeting on 3 December 2020.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.agonasport.com/agonasport-allnews/epo-plans-to-submit-bid-to-host-uefa-europa-conference-league-final |title=EPO plans to submit bid to host UEFA Europa Conference League final |work=AGONAsport |date=28 December 2019 |access-date=12 August 2020 |archive-date=18 May 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210518101847/https://www.agonasport.com/agonasport-allnews/epo-plans-to-submit-bid-to-host-uefa-europa-conference-league-final |url-status=dead }}</ref> However, UEFA later decided to reopen the bidding process after appointing the host for the 2022 final only. Member associations had until 30 September 2021 to confirm their intention to submit a bid, while the bids must be submitted by 23 February 2022.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/026b-12db5fe4be55-4737379124d7-1000/20210726_circular_2021_55_en.zip |title=Invitation to bid for 2022/23 UEFA Europa Conference League final |magazine=UEFA Circular |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |number=55/2021 |date=26 July 2021 |access-date=3 November 2021}}</ref> Six associations expressed interest in hosting the final.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.idnes.cz/fotbal/pohary/praha-finale-konferencni-evropska-liga-kandidatura-2023.A211005_174516_fot_pohary_ten |title=Konferenční liga s vrcholem v Praze? V roce 2023 chce finále šest zemí |trans-title=Conference League with a peak in Prague? In 2023, six countries want the final |website=iDNES.cz |date=5 October 2021 |access-date=10 May 2022 |language=cs}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.gazzetta.gr/football/europa-conference-league/2089960/aek-katatethike-o-fakelos-gia-ton-teliko-toy-conference |title=ΑΕΚ: Κατατέθηκε ο φάκελος για τον τελικό του Conference League 2023 στην «Αγιά Σοφιά – OPAP Arena» |trans-title=AEK: The file for the final of Conference League 2023 was submitted to "Agia Sofia – OPAP Arena" |website=gazzetta.gr |date=10 February 2022 |access-date=10 May 2022 |language=el}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/60994485 |title=Europa Conference League: Irish FA bids to host final at Windsor Park |work=[[BBC Sport]] |date=5 April 2022 |access-date=10 May 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://futbalsfz.sk/uefa-slovensky-futbalovy-zvaz-sa-uchadza-o-usporiadanie-finale-konferencnej-ligy/ |title=UEFA – Slovenský futbalový zväz sa uchádza o usporiadanie finále Európskej konferenčnej ligy |trans-title=UEFA – Slovak Football Association is bidding to host the final of the European Conference League |publisher=[[Slovak Football Association]] |date=6 October 2021 |access-date=10 May 2022 |language=sk}}</ref>

