==Post-match==
After the game Fiorentina president [[Rocco Commisso]] described West Ham  as treating Fiorentina players "like animals" after [[Luka Jović]] came off at half-time with a broken nose and Cristiano Biraghi received a bloodied face after being hit by an object thrown from the crowd.<ref>{{cite web | title=West Ham 'animals' in final - Fiorentina president | website=BBC Sport | date=8 June 2023 | url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65846514 | access-date=9 June 2023}}</ref>
UEFA later charged both clubs with "throwing of objects" with West Ham being charged with "invasion of the field of play" and Fiorentina being charged with the "lighting of fireworks".<ref>{{cite web | title=West Ham charged by Uefa for incidents in final | website=BBC Sport | date=9 June 2023 | url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65859842 | access-date=9 June 2023}}</ref> West Ham supporters were banned from attending the club's first away fixture of their [[2023–24 UEFA Europa League]] campaign. The club was also fined €50,000 after supporters threw objects onto the pitch and a further €8,000 for a pitch invasion following the game.<ref name=2024ban>{{cite web | title=West Ham fans banned for one European away game | website=BBC Sport | date=21 June 2023 | url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65978643 | access-date=21 June 2023}}</ref> Fiorentina were given a one-match ban for away supporters and were fined €30,000.<ref name="Football Italia 2023 t923">{{cite web | title=UEFA punish Fiorentina and West Ham after Conference League final fan trouble | website=Football Italia | date=21 June 2023 | url=https://football-italia.net/uefa-punish-fiorentina-and-west-ham-after-conference-league-final-fan-trouble/ | access-date=22 June 2023}}</ref>

On 8 June, thousands lined a route from the [[World Cup Sculpture|Champions Statue]] to [[Stratford Town Hall]] as West Ham players took part in an open top bus parade to show the trophy and celebrate the win.<ref>{{cite web | title=Thousands of fans watch West Ham trophy parade | website=BBC Sport | date=8 June 2023 | url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/65845801 | access-date=9 June 2023}}</ref>

